{:ev/id "inf-029" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757001740000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-passwords-0" {:concept-id "passwords" :kind :explanation :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "“whale-lantern-warm-umbrella” takes centuries to crack, P@ssw0rd1 minutes: dictionaries know every letter-for-symbol swap. Four random words that never share a phrase." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p4" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-030" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757001800000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-passwords-1" {:concept-id "passwords" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A forum password leaks, the same password guards your email: within an hour the attacker is in the mailbox, and from the mailbox every other password can be reset. That is why reuse is the policy's first prohibition." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p5" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-031" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757001860000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-password-manager-2" {:concept-id "password-manager" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "The master phrase opens the vault; everything else the manager generates and fills in itself. It even catches phishing: on a fake domain, autofill stays silent." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p7" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-032" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757001920000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-mfa-3" {:concept-id "mfa" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A password is known by two — you and, after a leak, the attacker. The app code exists only on your phone. Push fatigue is an attack too: never approve a sign-in you did not start." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p9" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-033" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757001980000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-mfa-4" {:concept-id "mfa" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "A push arrives at night: “Approve sign-in?”. You were not signing in — so someone already has the password. Decline, change the password, report: three steps, two minutes." :grounded-in "src-memo" :anchor "p3" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-034" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002040000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-social-engineering-5" {:concept-id "social-engineering" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "“This is the CFO, the payment must go out by 3 pm, don't tell the board” — urgency, authority and secrecy in one message. A real CFO survives a phone check." :grounded-in "src-memo" :anchor "p5" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-035" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002100000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-phishing-6" {:concept-id "phishing" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "The display name is written by the sender; only the address tells the truth. “IT Support <it-support@c0mpany-hr.net>” — read the domain right to left: the last part is the real one." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p11" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-036" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002160000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-phishing-7" {:concept-id "phishing" :kind :diagram :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "An annotated email with four flags: foreign sender domain, impersonal greeting, urgency timer, and a link whose visible text differs from the hover address." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p12" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-037" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002220000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-attachments-8" {:concept-id "attachments" :kind :explanation :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Invoice.pdf.exe is an executable wearing a PDF icon. Two extensions — trust the last one. Never enable office-file macros because the document asks you to." :grounded-in "src-memo" :anchor "p7" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-038" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002280000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-attachments-9" {:concept-id "attachments" :kind :worked-example :level :apprentice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "An email “from payroll” with a “salary portal” link. Hover: pay-roll.company.example.com.attacker.net. Read from the right: attacker.net. No click; forward to security." :grounded-in "src-memo" :anchor "p8" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-039" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002340000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-updates-10" {:concept-id "updates" :kind :explanation :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "“Remind me tomorrow” seven days in a row is a week with a publicly known hole. The reboot costs five minutes; incident cleanup costs weeks." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p14" :is :object}]]}
{:ev/id "inf-040" :ev/ns "demo" :ev/actor "demo-author" :ev/ts 1757002400000 :ev/type :change :ops [[:node-set "o-inf-device-lock-11" {:concept-id "device-lock" :kind :explanation :level :novice :locale "en" :origin :authored :text "Win+L or Ctrl+Cmd+Q — the habit for every time you stand up. An unlocked screen in an open office is your email, your access, and a message “from you” to anyone." :grounded-in "src-policy" :anchor "p16" :is :object}]]}
